## Closing answer

"I'd model Vehicle, Reservation and Invoice, with a `RentalService` coordinating search, reserve, pickup, return and cancel. Vehicle status describes the car now; reservations describe the future. Availability is an interval-overlap check on half-open ranges that include a one-hour cleaning buffer: two bookings clash when each starts before the other ends. Reserving re-checks and inserts under one lock per car, or a row lock in the database, so a car is never promised twice. Pricing is a strategy – per started day plus per started late hour. A late return blocks the next pickup, so I'd offer another car or a free cancellation."
